    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60206" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρουσ-τικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fit for striking, butting</i>, of a ram, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.113
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>able to sound the right note</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄργανα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					918a33
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. θίξις χορδῶν</span>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠθική</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.802f
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., of a
			rhetorician or sophist, <i>striking, impressive</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1379
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κ.</span>
			<i>striking eloquence</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Dem.Enc.</u>
				32
			</span></i>.</div>
